## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design a scalable, tenant-isolated CDC and schema evolution pipeline with robust governance, security, and rollback requirements.

## Key Concepts

- Change Data Capture (CDC) at cloud scale
- Per-tenant data isolation and architecture
- Schema drift detection and automated validation
- Backward-compatible migration strategies
- Data Catalog contract enforcement
- DLP-based PII masking and data protection
- Data Exchange for secure partner publishing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-logic: drift detection
function driftCheck(incomingSchema, currentSchema) {
  const changes = schemaDiff(incomingSchema, currentSchema);

  if (isBackwardCompatible(changes)) {
    generateMigration(changes);
    createSnapshot();
    applyMigration(changes);
  } else {
    alertSchemaViolation(changes);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes design for per-tenant data quality and schema evolution in a large-scale streaming pipeline, focusing on data catalog lineage, backward-compatible changes, drift detection, and rollback – all essential for production data platforms.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming data quality checks (null density, ranges, referential integrity)
- Per-tenant isolation in storage and compute
- Schema evolution with backward compatibility
- End-to-end lineage via Data Catalog
- Drift detection and tenant-specific rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal validator against a registry schema (conceptual)
function validateRecord(record, schema) {
  // assume 'schema' is loaded from Data Catalog
  const valid = ajv.validate(schema, record);
  if (!valid) throw new Error('Validation error: ' + ajv.errorsText());
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to test schema drift across tenants and automate remediation?
- How to handle late-arriving data and replays without breaking lineage?
- How to enforce tenant isolation at storage and compute layers?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a compliant, scalable streaming pipeline with multi-region resilience, per-tenant isolation, and strong data governance.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region BigQuery with per-tenant isolation
- Dataflow transforms + DLP-based masking/tokenization
- Data Catalog for lineage and data contracts versioning
- 24h per-tenant rollback via snapshots
- Schema evolution handling and drift alerts

## Code Example
```javascript
// High-level pseudo orchestrator (conceptual only)
function flow(tenantId, event) {
  const masked = mask(event, tenantId);
  writeToBigQuery(masked, { tenant: tenantId, region: selectRegion(tenantId) });
  logLineage(tenantId, event, masked);
}
```

